@*
    Risk Centre (migrations 169-172, 176, 204-207).
    Rendered from Manage.cshtml when Model.Key == "risk-centre".

    Two tabs, because the BRD has two things and they are not the same
    thing (BRD §3):

      Candidates     potential risks raised by a GRAC source, awaiting
                     the initial assessment (BRD: "Initial Risk Analysis") that §1 makes mandatory.
      Risk Register  the authoritative repository of risks that have
                     completed that assessment (§9).

    Two routes converge on the register (§4):
      A  Source -> Candidate -> Analysis -> Register
      B  Create Custom Risk (creation + analysis in one form) -> Register

    Route B lives on the Register tab, not the Candidates tab, because
    §4B is explicit that a custom risk has no candidate stage.
*@
@model PracticeManagement.Web.Models.PracticeScreen
@using PracticeManagement.Web.Security
@* ISession.GetString is an extension in this namespace, and neither
   Razor's implicit usings nor _ViewImports include it -- _Layout carries
   the same two lines for the same reason. Without it the @@{ } block
   below fails to compile with CS1061. *@
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http
@{
    // The signed-in user's employee id, rendered for the bulk accept
    // form to PRE-SELECT an accepter (295).
    //
    // Read from session in the view, the way _Layout already reads the
    // display name and organisation, rather than through a new
    // "who am I" endpoint -- the value is known at render time and a
    // round trip to learn it would be one we do not need.
    //
    // It is a DEFAULT ONLY, never an authority. The server stamps
    // actorEmployeeId from the session regardless of what the browser
    // sends, and sp_risk_acceptance_save still refuses an accepter from
    // another organisation (56608). Empty when the account is not mapped
    // to an employee, in which case the picker simply opens unset.
    var sessionEmployeeId = Context.Session.GetString(PracticeSessionIdentity.EmployeeIdKey);
}

@* Hidden while the Risk Analysis full page is open — that page carries
   its own heading naming the risk being analysed, and two page headings
   stacked on one screen reads as a rendering fault. *@
<div class="pm-page-heading compact" id="riskCentreHeading">
    <div>
        <p class="pm-eyebrow">@Model.Group / @Model.Title</p>
        <h1>@Model.Title</h1>
        <p>Assess before register. Risk candidates raised by Gap, Exception, Assurance, Obligation and other GRAC sources are assessed here before entering the Risk Register; authorised users can also create a custom risk directly.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="pm-tabs risk-tabs" role="tablist">
    <button type="button" class="risk-tab is-active" data-risk-tab="candidates" role="tab" aria-selected="true">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-inbox"></i> Risk Candidates
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="risk-tab" data-risk-tab="register" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-book"></i> Risk Register
    </button>
    @* BRD §23 — separate visibility for Candidates and Register, plus the
       §19 approval queue and the §21 notification outbox. *@
    @* Review Risk and Risk Calendar are two views of ONE column,
       next_review_date (migration 261):

         Review Risk    next_review_date <= today  -- the work queue
         Risk Calendar  next_review_date in a range -- the outlook

       They are separate tabs rather than one filtered grid because they
       answer different questions. "What must I look at now?" is a list
       you work through; "what is coming?" is a shape you scan. A single
       screen doing both does neither well. *@
    @* Accept Risk sits before Review Risk because that is the order the
       work happens in: a risk is accepted once, then comes back for
       review on a cadence. Its list is workflow_stage_code =
       'AcceptanceDue', which the view in 264 already computes -- so
       "ready to accept" means one thing here, on the register grid and
       in the dashboard, and no screen re-implements the test. *@
    <button type="button" class="risk-tab" data-risk-tab="accept" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check"></i> Accept Risk
        <span class="pm-badge risk-tab-badge" id="acceptDueBadge" hidden>0</span>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="risk-tab" data-risk-tab="review" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-rotate-left"></i> Review Risk
        <span class="pm-badge risk-tab-badge" id="reviewDueBadge" hidden>0</span>
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="risk-tab" data-risk-tab="calendar" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-calendar-days"></i> Risk Calendar
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="risk-tab" data-risk-tab="dashboard" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-chart-pie"></i> Dashboard
    </button>
    <button type="button" class="pm-button icon risk-tab-action" id="riskConfigBtn"
            title="Risk Centre settings" aria-label="Risk Centre settings">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-gear"></i>
    </button>
</div>

@* The organisation picker appears in EVERY tab's filter row, not in a
   bar of its own and not in only one tab.

   Originally it lived in the Candidates toolbar alone, inside
   #riskListView — which showTab() hides on Register and Dashboard. On
   those tabs the control was not on the page at all, so whatever
   organisation init() auto-selected was the only one reachable, and a
   register holding rows for another organisation read as "no risks match
   these filters" with no way to correct it.

   Lifting it out to its own bar fixed the reachability but took it out of
   the filter row, where it belongs and where operators look for it. So
   each toolbar carries its own control instead, all marked
   .risk-org-filter. They are three views of ONE value: changing any of
   them sets state.organizationId and syncs the others. Distinct ids
   because duplicate ids are invalid; the class is what the JS binds to. *@

@* ================= Tab 1 — Risk Candidates (BRD §6, §16) ============ *@
<section class="pm-panel" id="riskListView" hidden>
    <div class="pm-toolbar">
        <select id="riskFilterOrganization" class="risk-org-filter" title="Organization"><option value="">Select organization</option></select>
        <select id="riskFilterStatus">
            <option value="">All statuses</option>
            @* 'Pending' is the stored code for BRD §16 "New" — see migration 205. *@
            <option value="Pending" selected>New</option>
            <option value="UnderAnalysis">Under assessment</option>
            <option value="ClarificationRequired">Clarification required</option>
            <option value="AnalysisCompleted">Assessment completed</option>
            <option value="Registered">Registered</option>
            <option value="Rejected">Rejected</option>
            <option value="ClosedAsDuplicate">Closed as duplicate</option>
            <option value="Withdrawn">Withdrawn</option>
            <option value="Accepted">Accepted (legacy)</option>
        </select>
        <select id="riskFilterSource"><option value="">All sources</option></select>
        <button class="pm-button icon" id="riskRefreshBtn" type="button" title="Refresh" aria-label="Refresh">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate"></i>
        </button>
    </div>

    <div class="pm-table-wrap">
        <table id="riskTable">
            @* Analyst and Att columns dropped from the Risk Candidates grid
               (change request 2026-09-22) -- display only. assignedAnalystName
               and attachmentCount are still on the row data and still used
               elsewhere (e.g. the candidate detail modal / analysis form);
               they are just no longer columns here. See risk-centre.js's
               refresh() for the matching row markup and displayCandidateTitle()
               for the "Risk: " prefix strip (display only -- the stored
               candidate_title is untouched). *@
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Candidate</th>
                    <th>Source</th>
                    <th>Rating</th>
                    <th>Identified</th>
                    <th>Status</th>
                    <th>Registered risk</th>
                    <th aria-label="Actions"></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="riskTableBody">
                <tr><td colspan="7" class="pm-empty-row">Select an organization to load candidates.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    @* Standard grid pager (pm-grid.js). Server-side: the page
       controls refetch, they never slice a local array. *@
    <div id="candPager"></div>
</section>

@* ================= Tab 2 — Risk Register (BRD §9, §17, §23) ========= *@
<section class="pm-panel" id="riskRegisterView" hidden>
    <div class="pm-toolbar">
        <select id="regFilterOrganization" class="risk-org-filter" title="Organization"><option value="">Select organization</option></select>
        @* The Record status filter was removed: the Stage filter below
           is the lifecycle control now, and two dropdowns asking almost
           the same question is what this review set out to end.

           NOTE THE SIDE EFFECT, IT IS THE POINT. That dropdown defaulted
           to `Active`, so the register was silently showing ONLY risks
           with status_code = 'Active' — a risk moved to UnderTreatment,
           Accepted or Monitoring vanished from the default view. With no
           status filter, sp_risk_register_list receives @status_code =
           NULL and lists every risk, which is what a register should do.
           Closed and Retired now list too; Stage = Closed isolates them.

           @status_code is untouched on the procedure and the API — only
           this control is gone. *@
        <select id="regFilterSource"><option value="">All sources</option></select>
        <select id="regFilterCategory"><option value="">All categories</option></select>
        <select id="regFilterRating">
            <option value="">All ratings</option>
            <option value="Critical">Critical</option>
            <option value="High">High</option>
            <option value="Medium">Medium</option>
            <option value="Low">Low</option>
        </select>
        @* A registered risk with no rating is outstanding work, not bad
           data — so it is filterable, not hidden. *@
        <select id="regFilterPending">
            <option value="">Scored and unscored</option>
            <option value="1">Analysis pending</option>
            <option value="0">Analysis done</option>
        </select>
        @* The derived stage (migration 264). Filtering on it is how the
           register answers "what is waiting on me?" without the user
           having to know which combination of status, pending flags and
           task counts adds up to each answer. *@
        <select id="regFilterStage" title="Workflow stage">
            <option value="">All stages</option>
            <option value="AnalysisDue">Analysis due</option>
            <option value="TreatmentDue">Treatment option due</option>
            <option value="InTreatment">In treatment</option>
            <option value="ResidualDue">Residual analysis due</option>
            <option value="AcceptanceDue">Acceptance due</option>
            <option value="Accepted">Accepted</option>
            <option value="ReviewDue">Review due</option>
            <option value="Closed">Closed</option>
        </select>
        <select id="regFilterTreatment" title="Treatment option">
            <option value="">All treatment options</option>
            <option value="Terminate">Terminate / Avoid</option>
            <option value="Treat">Treat / Reduce</option>
            <option value="Transfer">Transfer / Share</option>
            <option value="Tolerate">Tolerate / Accept</option>
        </select>
        <input type="search" id="regFilterSearch" placeholder="Search title / statement / RSK-..." />
        <button class="pm-button icon" id="regRefreshBtn" type="button" title="Refresh" aria-label="Refresh">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate"></i>
        </button>
        @* BRD §4B / §11 — Route B lives here, next to the register it feeds. *@
        <button class="pm-button primary" id="regCustomBtn" type="button">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i> Create custom risk
        </button>
    </div>

    <div class="pm-table-wrap">
        <table id="regTable">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    @* COLUMN ORDER AND SET (change request, 2026-09-23):
                       Risk ID, Risk, Owner, Stage, Inherent Risk Score,
                       Residual Risk Score, Next Review Date -- exactly
                       these seven, in this order. Category and Source
                       (previously columns 3-4) are REMOVED from this
                       grid on the same request -- both are still on the
                       risk detail view and still drive their own
                       filters (regFilterCategory / regFilterSource,
                       untouched) and the dashboard drill-down, only the
                       grid columns are gone. Owner moved up from the end
                       (was after Next review); Stage moved up ahead of
                       the two score columns (was after them). *@
                    <th>Risk ID</th>
                    <th>Risk</th>
                    <th>Owner</th>
                    @* THE STAGE COLUMN (migration 264).
                       Derived, never stored — vw_pm_risk_workflow_stage
                       computes it from analysis_pending, the treatment
                       option, the open task count, residual_pending,
                       accepted_dt and next_review_date. It cannot
                       disagree with the columns beside it because there
                       is nothing to keep in sync.

                       Stage is now the ONLY progress column. Treatment,
                       Scope, Status and Registered were removed on
                       request; Stage subsumes most of what Treatment and
                       Status showed, because it is derived from the
                       treatment option and the open task count in the
                       first place. Every removed value is still on the
                       risk detail view — none of them were dropped from
                       the payload, only from this grid. *@
                    <th>Stage</th>
                    @* TWO RATINGS, DELIBERATELY (migration 258).
                       Inherent is the score BEFORE treatment; Residual is
                       what is left AFTER it. Both are resolved from the
                       same matrix by the same procedure, so the columns
                       are comparable — which is the only reason showing
                       them side by side is honest. *@
                    <th>Inherent Risk Score</th>
                    <th>Residual Risk Score</th>
                    <th>Next Review Date</th>
                    <th aria-label="Actions"></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="regTableBody">
                <tr><td colspan="8" class="pm-empty-row">Select an organization to load the register.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    @* Standard grid pager (pm-grid.js). Server-side: the page
       controls refetch, they never slice a local array. *@
    <div id="regPager"></div>
</section>

@* ============ Tab 3 — Accept Risk (migration 295) ==================
    Everything waiting to be accepted, in one place, accepted singly or
    in bulk.

    THE LIST IS NOT A NEW QUERY. It is the register filtered to
    workflowStageCode=AcceptanceDue -- the stage vw_pm_risk_workflow_stage
    (264) already computes as "Tolerate chosen, or the residual
    assessment is done, and not yet accepted". Writing a second
    definition of "ready to accept" here would give the tab, the register
    grid and the dashboard three chances to disagree about the same
    question.

    The toggle switches that one filter to Accepted, so the person who
    just accepted twelve risks can see them without leaving the tab.
    Same grid, same endpoint, one query-string value different.

    SINGLE ACCEPT IS THE EXISTING PAGE. The Accept button on each row
    opens the very same #riskAcceptancePageView the register and
    residual pages open, with its own guidance banner and its own rules.
    The tab adds a way to REACH acceptance, not a second way to DO it.
=================================================================== *@
<section class="pm-panel" id="riskAcceptView" hidden>
    <div class="pm-toolbar">
        <select id="accFilterOrganization" class="risk-org-filter" title="Organization"><option value="">Select organization</option></select>
        <select id="accFilterOwner"><option value="">All owners</option></select>
        <select id="accFilterRating">
            <option value="">All ratings</option>
            <option value="Critical">Critical</option>
            <option value="High">High</option>
            <option value="Medium">Medium</option>
            <option value="Low">Low</option>
        </select>
        <label class="risk-inline-label">
            Show
            <select id="accFilterStage">
                <option value="AcceptanceDue" selected>Pending acceptance</option>
                <option value="Accepted">Already accepted</option>
            </select>
        </label>
        <input type="search" id="accFilterSearch" placeholder="Search title / statement / RSK-..." />
        <button class="pm-button icon" id="accRefreshBtn" type="button" title="Refresh" aria-label="Refresh">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate"></i>
        </button>
    </div>

    <div class="pm-table-wrap">
        @* Same pattern as the review tab's bar: hidden until something
           is selected, because a permanent "0 selected" toolbar is
           furniture. *@
        <div class="risk-bulkbar" id="accBulkBar" hidden>
            <span id="accBulkCount">0 selected</span>
            <button type="button" class="pm-button primary" id="accBulkAcceptBtn">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check" aria-hidden="true"></i> Accept selected
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="accBulkClearBtn">Clear selection</button>
        </div>

        <table id="accTable">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th style="width:28px;">
                        <input type="checkbox" id="accSelectAll"
                               title="Select all rows shown"
                               aria-label="Select all rows shown" />
                    </th>
                    <th>Risk ID</th>
                    <th>Risk</th>
                    <th>Owner</th>
                    <th>Inherent</th>
                    <th>Residual</th>
                    <th>Treatment</th>
                    <th>Accepted</th>
                    <th>Next review</th>
                    <th aria-label="Actions"></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="accTableBody">
                <tr><td colspan="10" class="pm-empty-row">Select an organization to load risks awaiting acceptance.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    <div id="accPager"></div>
</section>

@* ================= Tab 4 — Review Risk (migration 264) =============
    Risks whose review date has arrived.

    THE RULE IS ONE LINE AND THE SCREEN DOES NOT RESTATE IT:
        next_review_date <= today, and the risk is not Closed/Retired.

    Future dates do not appear here at all. The "Show upcoming" control
    widens the horizon by passing includeFutureDays, which the SAME
    procedure honours — so the due list and the upcoming list can never
    disagree about what counts as due, because there is only one query.
================================================================== *@
<section class="pm-panel" id="riskReviewView" hidden>
    <div class="pm-toolbar">
        <select id="revFilterOrganization" class="risk-org-filter" title="Organization"><option value="">Select organization</option></select>
        <select id="revFilterOwner"><option value="">All owners</option></select>
        <select id="revFilterRating">
            <option value="">All ratings</option>
            <option value="Critical">Critical</option>
            <option value="High">High</option>
            <option value="Medium">Medium</option>
            <option value="Low">Low</option>
        </select>
        <label class="risk-inline-label">
            Horizon
            <select id="revFilterHorizon">
                <option value="" selected>Due and overdue only</option>
                <option value="7">+ next 7 days</option>
                <option value="30">+ next 30 days</option>
                <option value="90">+ next 90 days</option>
            </select>
        </label>
        <input type="search" id="revFilterSearch" placeholder="Search title / statement / RSK-..." />
        <button class="pm-button icon" id="revRefreshBtn" type="button" title="Refresh" aria-label="Refresh">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate"></i>
        </button>
    </div>

    <div class="pm-table-wrap">
        @* Bulk review bar. Hidden until something is selected -- a
           permanently visible "0 selected" toolbar is furniture. *@
        <div class="risk-bulkbar" id="revBulkBar" hidden>
            <span id="revBulkCount">0 selected</span>
            <button type="button" class="pm-button primary" id="revBulkReviewBtn">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-list-check" aria-hidden="true"></i> Bulk review
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="pm-button" id="revBulkClearBtn">Clear selection</button>
        </div>

        <table id="revTable">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th style="width:28px;">
                        <input type="checkbox" id="revSelectAll"
                               title="Select all rows shown"
                               aria-label="Select all rows shown" />
                    </th>
                    <th>Risk ID</th>
                    <th>Risk</th>
                    <th>Owner</th>
                    <th>Inherent</th>
                    <th>Residual</th>
                    <th>Treatment</th>
                    <th>Accepted</th>
                    <th>Review date</th>
                    <th>Overdue</th>
                    <th aria-label="Actions"></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="revTableBody">
                <tr><td colspan="11" class="pm-empty-row">Select an organization to load risks due for review.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    @* Standard grid pager (pm-grid.js). Server-side: the page
       controls refetch, they never slice a local array. *@
    <div id="revPager"></div>
</section>

@* ================= Tab 5 — Risk Calendar (migration 264) ===========
    The same next_review_date column, laid out as a month.

    A SEPARATE, SMALL CALENDAR AND NOT Practice/Calendar:
    the assurance calendar is a 1,100-line month/week/day view wired to
    assurance_calendar_events, a materialised schedule with rules and
    overrides. A risk review date is one mutable column with no schedule
    behind it. Generalising that calendar to carry both would mean
    maintaining schedule machinery for something that has none, and
    would put the assurance module at risk for a Risk Centre feature.

    So this is a month grid, it borrows practice-calendar.css's visual
    language, and it does one thing.
================================================================== *@
<section class="pm-panel" id="riskCalendarView" hidden>
    <div class="pm-toolbar">
        <select id="calFilterOrganization" class="risk-org-filter" title="Organization"><option value="">Select organization</option></select>
        <select id="calFilterOwner"><option value="">All owners</option></select>
        <button class="pm-button icon" id="calPrevBtn" type="button" title="Previous month" aria-label="Previous month">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-left"></i>
        </button>
        <span class="risk-cal-title" id="calTitle">&nbsp;</span>
        <button class="pm-button icon" id="calNextBtn" type="button" title="Next month" aria-label="Next month">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right"></i>
        </button>
        <button class="pm-button" id="calTodayBtn" type="button">Today</button>
        <span class="pm-hint" id="calSummary"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="risk-cal">
        <div class="risk-cal-head">
            <div>Mon</div><div>Tue</div><div>Wed</div><div>Thu</div>
            <div>Fri</div><div>Sat</div><div>Sun</div>
        </div>
        <div class="risk-cal-grid" id="calGrid"></div>
    </div>

    <h3 class="risk-subhead">Reviews in this month</h3>
    <div class="pm-table-wrap">
        <table id="calListTable">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Review date</th><th>Risk ID</th><th>Risk</th>
                    <th>Rating</th><th>Owner</th><th>Treatment</th><th aria-label="Actions"></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="calListBody">
                <tr><td colspan="7" class="pm-empty-row">Select an organization to load the calendar.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>

@* ================= Tab 6 — Dashboard (BRD §19, §21, §23) =========== *@
<section class="pm-panel" id="riskDashboardView" hidden>
    <div class="pm-toolbar">
        <select id="dashFilterOrganization" class="risk-org-filter" title="Organization"><option value="">Select organization</option></select>
        <label class="risk-inline-label">
            Trend window
            <select id="dashTrendMonths">
                <option value="6">6 months</option>
                <option value="12" selected>12 months</option>
                <option value="24">24 months</option>
            </select>
        </label>
        <button class="pm-button icon" id="dashRefreshBtn" type="button" title="Refresh" aria-label="Refresh">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-arrows-rotate"></i>
        </button>
    </div>

    @* --- Risk Candidates block (§23) --- *@
    <h3 class="risk-subhead">Risk candidates</h3>
    <div class="risk-tiles" id="dashCandidateTiles"></div>

    @* --- Approval queue (§19) --- *@
    <h3 class="risk-subhead">Awaiting approval</h3>
    <div class="pm-table-wrap">
        <table id="approvalTable">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Candidate</th><th>Risk statement</th><th>Category</th>
                    <th>Rating</th><th>Owner</th><th>Analysed</th><th>Waiting</th>
                    <th aria-label="Actions"></th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody id="approvalTableBody">
                <tr><td colspan="8" class="pm-empty-row">Nothing awaiting approval.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    @* Standard grid pager (pm-grid.js). Server-side: the page
       controls refetch, they never slice a local array. *@
    <div id="apprPager"></div>

    @* --- Candidate ageing (§23) --- *@
    <h3 class="risk-subhead">Candidate ageing <span class="pm-hint">(open candidates only)</span></h3>
    <div class="risk-two-col">
        <div class="risk-bars" id="dashAgeing"></div>
        <div class="pm-table-wrap">
            <table id="ageingTable">
                <thead>
                    <tr><th>Candidate</th><th>Source</th><th>Status</th><th>Analyst</th><th>Age</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody id="ageingTableBody">
                    <tr><td colspan="5" class="pm-empty-row">No open candidates.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* --- Risk Register block (§23) --- *@
    <h3 class="risk-subhead">Risk register</h3>
    <div class="risk-tiles" id="dashRegisterTiles"></div>

    <div class="risk-grid-4">
        <div><h4 class="risk-subhead">By rating</h4>       <div class="risk-bars" id="dashByRating"></div></div>
        <div><h4 class="risk-subhead">By category</h4>     <div class="risk-bars" id="dashByCategory"></div></div>
        <div><h4 class="risk-subhead">By source</h4>       <div class="risk-bars" id="dashBySource"></div></div>
        <div><h4 class="risk-subhead">By business unit</h4><div class="risk-bars" id="dashByUnit"></div></div>
        <div><h4 class="risk-subhead">By owner</h4>        <div class="risk-bars" id="dashByOwner"></div></div>
        <div><h4 class="risk-subhead">Candidates by source</h4><div class="risk-bars" id="dashCandBySource"></div></div>
    </div>

    @* --- Trend (§23) --- *@
    <h3 class="risk-subhead">Risk trend</h3>
